@startuml
title KiwiDB — State Machine: Flush slot (event-chain ordering)
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Pending : slot built for a snapshot\n(position in the ordered batch)

Pending --> Aborted : batch_abort already set\n(a predecessor failed)
Pending --> Writing : acquire semaphore permit

state Writing {
  [*] --> WritingSSTable
  WritingSSTable --> WritingSSTable : write data/index/filter/meta
}
note right of Writing
  PHASE 1 — multiple slots
  write in parallel (bounded
  by the semaphore).
end note

Writing --> WaitingToCommit : write done\n(release permit)
Writing --> Failed : exception during write

WaitingToCommit --> WaitingToCommit : await prev_committed
WaitingToCommit --> Aborted : batch_abort set\n(close reader, skip)
WaitingToCommit --> Committing : prev committed & not aborted

state Committing {
  [*] --> Registering
  Registering --> Registering : commit to SSTableManager,\npop snapshot, truncate WAL,\ntrigger compaction check
}
note right of Committing
  PHASE 2 — commits run
  strictly in slot order.
end note

Committing --> Committed : set my_committed\n(pass baton to next slot)

Failed --> Aborted : set batch_abort\n(signal downstream)
Aborted --> [*] : ALWAYS set my_committed\n(prevents chain deadlock)
Committed --> [*]

@enduml
